WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.730
- She's made headlines this year

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:03.437
for using her charitable initiative

00:00:03.437 --> 00:00:06.520
"Be Strong" to get millions,

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:09.990
millions of PPE items
delivered to medical workers

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:12.970
in all 50 States!

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:17.570
(audience cheers)
Bethenny, you were first here.

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:20.500
There were a few people
that jumped in first.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:21.510
You were one of them.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:23.150
How did you do it?

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:24.640
- We always jump in first.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.570
It's a disaster relief initiative

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:28.090
and you have to just have that sort of

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:30.300
run and gun type of personality.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.630
It's extremely intense

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:34.210
and you have to have
an intense personality

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:35.370
and you can't wait

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:37.130
because it's too late if you wait.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:40.990
So, and you have to
navigate a lot of corruption

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:43.990
and counterfeit PPE.

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:46.577
We did $20 million of PPE,

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:50.850
over $20 million of PPE for COVID.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:54.210
And we did in excess of 2 million units,

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:56.560
we did over a million hazmat suits

00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:00.360
and over a million masks to all 50 States.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.473
(audience cheers)
- I mean, come on!

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:05.860
When we're all sitting
there in fear, immovable-

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:06.693
- [Bethenny] I know.

00:01:06.693 --> 00:01:08.790
- You got up there and took action!

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:10.740
- [Bethenny] It's crazy!
- It is so impressive!

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:11.870
It's inspiring!

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:14.004
- [Bethenny] Thank you.
- It's incentivizing!

00:01:14.004 --> 00:01:17.090
Okay, so, your podcast "Just Be",

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:22.090
you talk to a lot of really
respectable doers out there.

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:25.730
I was blown away by the caliber
of people, very focused.

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:27.020
- I kept the caliber tight.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.340
It's not about being
the most famous person.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:31.540
It's about being someone who is a baller,

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:33.670
who's a gangster, who's done it,

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:35.560
who started from the
bottom, now they're here,

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:37.470
a visionary, a game changer.

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:39.830
And, there's a rant in the
beginning where I'm a moron

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:41.240
and talk about the minutia that

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:42.550
I just think about it in my head.

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:43.870
And that sort of a little bit of humor.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.828
- Well, comedy and humanizing
things is a good thing.

00:01:45.828 --> 00:01:46.750
- Yeah, it's a little bit of humor

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:49.830
and crazy story about
SIA and just insane story

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:51.390
about Gary Cohn, who worked with Trump.

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:53.360
Like, just crazy stories
that have happened to me.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:55.030
But then we get into the meat, which is,

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:56.710
it's not foreplay, it's the main act.

00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:58.920
It's like, listen, people are giving me,

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:01.100
Mark Cuban's giving me
an hour of his time,

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.850
Paris Hilton, an hour of their day.

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:03.840
That's like dog years.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:04.950
That's a lot of time for them.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:07.690
They're so busy and
they're giving the tools,

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:10.400
the keys to the kingdom, how
they think, how they operate.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:11.800
And there are so many threads

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:13.750
between all of these successful people.

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:14.700
They could be so different

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.400
but they have the similar work ethic.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.160
They have a similar way
of thinking about things,

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.430
decision making and I
have threads with them.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:23.840
And so people at home can
collect all this information

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:25.500
and use that for themselves to be

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:27.290
whatever type of entrepreneur,

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:30.340
or successful mom, or business person,

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:31.680
whatever they wanna be.

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:34.210
I mean, this is true access

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:37.950
to information that can be a
game changer for your life.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:41.220
And you have already been an
inspiration to many people.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:44.040
And, actually I have a surprise.

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:47.090
There is someone here
who wants to thank you,

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:50.040
especially because of the entrepreneurial

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:53.660
inspiration and courage
that you gave to her.

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:55.330
So, she is an entrepreneur

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:58.281
and a mother of three,
please welcome Lauren Levy.

00:02:58.281 --> 00:03:01.054
(audience cheers)
Hi Lauren!

00:03:01.054 --> 00:03:02.319
- Hi!
- [Drew] Welcome!

00:03:02.319 --> 00:03:03.747
- [Bethenny] How are you?
(Lauren screams)

00:03:03.747 --> 00:03:04.580
- Hi!
- [Drew] By the way,

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:05.413
I just wanna say,

00:03:05.413 --> 00:03:07.900
this is the first time
we've had three women

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:10.450
at this desk, so I'm very excited.

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:12.050
This is a real moment for our show.

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:13.314
- You look beautiful!
- Thank you!

00:03:13.314 --> 00:03:14.147
- How are you?

00:03:14.147 --> 00:03:16.600
- I'm so excited to meet you, both of you!

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:17.830
This is like a dream come true!

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:19.770
- Lauren, I would like
you to tell Bethenny

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:22.900
about your company because
I'm freaking out at the

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:26.700
sort of unique approach that you have

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:30.700
and being parents and where
you also have an end game

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:33.970
for this as far as like,
it's a full life circle

00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:34.880
plan that you have.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:36.890
I am blown away by your business concept!

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:38.590
Will you share it with Bethenny?

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:42.590
- Sure, so, Magnetic Me is
a lifestyle apparel brand

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:45.240
that I founded about 10 years ago.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:49.200
And we make so safe,
magnetic fastening clothing

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.090
to make you know, getting dressed easy.

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:54.020
So there's no snaps,
no buttons, no zippers.

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:55.330
We initially started with baby

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:58.770
and now we do nursing and
we're expanding and growing.

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:02.200
- And you're also providing
it for people with arthritis.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:05.030
So, for parents who have babies-

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:06.340
- [Bethenny] Smart, smart!
- I know!

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:09.330
This is, I mean, I think
your business model

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:11.230
is extraordinary!

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:13.390
I work with a woman, Dr. Aliza Pressman,

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:16.320
and we were just doing a thing
for Domino Magazine for kids.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:17.153
And it's like,

00:04:17.153 --> 00:04:19.330
put the mirrors where
they're dressing themselves

00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:20.610
at their level.

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:23.070
You do not hang mirrors at your eye level.

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:25.780
You give them clothing that can snap

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:27.330
you know, in a certain way,

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:30.250
so that it incentivized them
to become their own dressers.

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:33.020
Parents with babies,
they're running around.

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:35.480
It's so hard to keep it all intact.

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:37.720
This is a real game changer.

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:38.910
And then, the way that you're helping

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:41.460
also people who need the help.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.420
I just think your business
model's so interesting!

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:44.253
- [Bethenny] It's amazing!
- [Lauren] Thank you!

00:04:44.253 --> 00:04:45.086
- [Bethenny] Yes, it's unique.

00:04:45.086 --> 00:04:48.550
- It's great for, we call
them, "No Drama Pajamas"

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:50.390
for toddlers who hate getting,

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.400
you know, clothing over their heads.

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:53.950
- [Drew] How about no
drama for the parents?

00:04:53.950 --> 00:04:54.783
I mean, I've like,

00:04:54.783 --> 00:04:57.430
I've lost my mind trying
to dress two kids.

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:58.960
- Yeah, the nightly struggle is real.

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:02.140
So, we have a little magnetic
fastener and opens wide.

00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:02.973
- [Bethenny] That's perfect!

00:05:02.973 --> 00:05:04.820
- [Drew] Did you have
a question for Bethenny

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:06.790
on any advice?
- Yeah, so,

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:08.824
I'm so inspired by you!

00:05:08.824 --> 00:05:12.830
I come from such humble
beginnings, like you do!

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:16.160
Our stories are like, remarkably similar

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:18.520
and I've just watched you, you know

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:22.290
your sheer will and your
grit and your determination.

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:24.270
And it's really been such a pleasure

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:27.090
and just so inspiring
watching your journey.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:28.200
- [Bethenny] Thank you.
- I just wanted to

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:29.220
say thank you.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:30.980
And like, your highs and your lows

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:33.400
and you know, through
starting Magnetic Me,

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:36.930
it's just been great
watching somebody do it.

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:38.400
- It's hard to do!
- It's hard.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:39.590
- It's hard to do at any level.

00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:40.730
It's hard to do at any,

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:42.740
even though I've been on television,

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:44.010
you have to be relentless.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.780
You have to be focused, laser focused

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:48.810
and just it's about old school hard work.

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:50.120
That's the key to success, the old school.

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:52.210
- And now, you're also an amazing mom

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:54.360
and a mogul, but you're
also a philanthropist.

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:58.337
And, we're looking to start
a non-for-profit called,

00:05:58.337 --> 00:06:00.240
"Big to Little, Little to Big"

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:02.810
where parents or anyone
who buys our clothing

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:06.580
can use it and then send it
back and we can up-cycle it

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:09.170
to, you know, struggling
or needy families.

00:06:09.170 --> 00:06:10.003
- [Bethenny] Oh wow!

00:06:10.003 --> 00:06:10.836
That's amazing!
- Yeah.

00:06:10.836 --> 00:06:11.669
- And that's perfect actually!

00:06:11.669 --> 00:06:13.160
That's good for disaster relief too.

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:15.360
There's like, that's a very big need.

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:18.210
I would say the key to, for me,

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:20.600
the key to philanthropy
and why it's connected

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:21.530
and it's been so successful,

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:23.290
because I was a nobody starting and no,

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:24.750
even though I was a
successful business woman

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:25.990
no one was trusting me in this space.

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:28.020
I couldn't get flip flops

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:30.920
or rain boots for the first,
for the hurricane Harvey.

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:32.220
But I just hustled.

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:34.660
As I do with business,

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:36.230
you have to be totally transparent

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:38.060
and take people through the story.

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:39.360
This is what we're planning to do.

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:40.900
This is how we're planning to do it.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:42.740
If it shifts, it could
have been when we were

00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:44.560
in The Bahamas or the Amazon fires,

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:47.510
we're trying to get planes
to shower water over there.

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:49.480
But then we had to change it.

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:52.870
First, it was sanitizing kits for COVID

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:55.820
and then it became, "Okay,
we're letting everyone know."

00:06:55.820 --> 00:06:56.653
You're not perfect.

00:06:56.653 --> 00:06:59.180
And in the moment, you
have to be very transparent

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:01.830
and people have to understand
exactly where their money

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:02.710
or whatever, you know,

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:04.710
if they're donating
money, where it is going.

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:06.670
So, every dollar is important

00:07:06.670 --> 00:07:09.310
and philanthropy has
become so not transparent.

00:07:09.310 --> 00:07:11.420
People have no idea what
percentage is being taken.

00:07:11.420 --> 00:07:14.040
We give 100% to the effort and we explain

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:16.550
that you gave a dollar,
it went to buy this bowl.

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:17.940
This is where your dollar went.

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:19.230
You gave a hundred thousand dollars.

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:20.600
It went to help all these people.

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:22.050
People wanna feel that it's personal,

00:07:22.050 --> 00:07:24.030
just like in business.

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:25.560
If you're investing your money

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:28.390
you wanna know where exactly is it going?

00:07:28.390 --> 00:07:29.900
Am I getting a return on my investment?

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:31.653
And, that's the key to it in my opinion.

00:07:31.653 --> 00:07:32.486
(audience cheers)

00:07:32.486 --> 00:07:34.470
- I think there are so many secrets

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:37.555
by the way, we're gonna
put you up on our website.

00:07:37.555 --> 00:07:38.388
- Thank you!
- [Drew] I would love

00:07:38.388 --> 00:07:39.530
to support your brand!

00:07:39.530 --> 00:07:41.498
We can sidebar and ask questions.

00:07:41.498 --> 00:07:43.323
Thank you Lauren, thank you Bethenny!

00:07:43.323 --> 00:07:44.314
- [Lauren] Thank you!

00:07:44.314 --> 00:07:46.897
(upbeat music)

